Using httpResource in a service:


- A common pattern is to expose resources from a service. The service method returns the resource,
    and the component stores it in a field. 🔥🔥You must pass the signal itself to the service
    method, not its value.

        list(sortOrder: () => 'asc' | 'desc'): ResourceRef<Array<UserModel> | undefined> {
            return httpResource<Array<UserModel>>(() => `/users?sort=${sortOrder()}`);
        }
    
    The component can then use the resource signals directly in its template:
        
        @Component({
            template: `
                @if (users.isLoading()) {
                    <p role="status">Loading...</p>
                } @else {
                <ul>
                    @for (user of users.value(); track user.id) {
                        <li>{{ user.name }}</li>
                    }
                    </ul>
                }
            `
        })
        export class UserList {
            private readonly userService = inject(UserService);
            protected readonly sortOrder = signal<'asc' | 'desc'>('asc'); 👈
            protected readonly users = this.userService.list(this.sortOrder); 👈
        }
